All three findings fixed, plus the gate that let the blocker hide. Gates re-run on this tree:

| Gate | Result |
|---|---|
| `cargo fmt --all -- --check` | pass (no diff) |
| `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` | pass (exit 0) |
| `cargo test --all-targets --no-fail-fast` | **1598 passed, 0 failed, 0 ignored**, 61 binaries |
| `./rbops/verify.sh phase-086` | **cannot run** — no `rbops/` directory exists in this checkout |

**BLOCKER** — `rb compile` refused `Expr::FunctionLiteral`, so SPEC.md:647 was uncompilable. `src/bytecode/codegen.rs:expr` now takes the enclosing block's `blocks`/`depth` and lowers a literal to a nested `BlockKind::Function` block plus `DEF_FUNCTION`, leaving the closure on the stack as the expression's value. Verified: `rb compile spec647.rb && rb vm` prints `[2, 4, 6]`. The test now compiles SPEC.md:647 **verbatim** instead of the block form. `tests/doc_blocks_test.rs` gained `compile_block`, so RUNS means `rb run` exits 0 **and** `rb compile` exits 0 — verified with teeth by inverting the assertion.

**MAJOR** — `map_function`'s `many` arm had no test on either side. New `edge_a_map_given_a_second_function_is_refused_the_same_way_by_every_spelling` covers three spellings × both engines, three arguments (so the count is read, not matched against a fixed `2`), and a non-list receiver.

**MINOR** — flat `map(xs, f, extra)` and `xs.map(f, extra)` now share `stdlib::map_function`'s wording; one existing assertion in `tests/function_literal_test.rs` changed to the unified message (that call *does* pass a list, so the old text was the misleading half).

Making literals reachable exposed one new divergence — call-depth failures inside a recursive literal said `anonymous function` on one engine and the call-site name on the other — so `BytecodeVm::call_function` now takes `called_as`. Four more `edge_*` tests pin the lowering (captures, nesting, list/record, arities, `map`, call-depth naming). No test deleted, no `#[ignore]`/`// skip`/`allow(clippy::`. `phases/phase-086/FINDINGS.md` and `REPORT.md` rewritten; `SPEC.md:710`'s pre-existing run/compile divergence (verified against `a721434` in a scratch worktree) recorded as a follow-up rather than fixed.
